\details{
A \code{merch_result} contains measurement tables and a \code{run_metadata} list. Shared fields
keep the same meaning wherever they appear. Returned fields
are calculated or copied from inputs, so they have no input default to fill.

There are no list columns in the result tables. Nested objects occur in the
recorded settings.

Length means feet in imperial calls and meters in metric calls. Diameter means
inches or centimeters. Physical volume means cubic feet or cubic meters.

The suffix \code{ib} means inside bark and \code{ob} means outside bark. Scaled quantities use
their own declared units. Values use the supplied currency.

No currency conversion or inventory expansion is performed. Output is not
rounded for display beyond the scaling procedure's rounding. }
